+- [ ] 1.3 Preserve present canonicalization behavior for every ineligible line and do not emit more than one alternate; verify existing canonicalization tests continue to pass.
+
+## 2. Retrieval and matcher integration
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Pass the eligible product-bearing alternate through the existing hybrid alternate-query path while retaining the normalized raw query as primary retrieval input; verify mocked dense/BM25 tests assert exactly one extra call only for a distinct eligible alternate and preserve deduplication/RRF behavior.
+- [ ] 2.2 Keep reranker input, `MatchResult.query`, caching, candidate limits, and final-selection semantics bound to the normalized original query; verify matcher tests with recording retriever/reranker for a mixed work-and-product line.
+- [ ] 2.3 Preserve fail-open behavior when alternate retrieval fails; verify a focused mocked retrieval test returns original-query candidates and no code path emits `NOT_FOUND` solely because a work cue was detected.
