+## Purpose
+
+Provide a safe additive retrieval representation for explicit products named inside tender work descriptions without claiming that a service request has a catalog product match.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Bound product-bearing retrieval alternate
+For a tender clause that explicitly contains both a recognized work action and a supported purchasable-product anchor, the system SHALL derive at most one distinct product-bearing retrieval alternate. The alternate MUST retain the anchored product phrase and its adjacent technical attributes, and it MUST be used in addition to, never in place of, the normalized original tender line.
+
+#### Scenario: Work description includes a product and dimensions
+- **WHEN** a tender clause requests a recognized work action for a supported product and gives product dimensions or execution details
+- **THEN** retrieval receives the original tender line and one alternate containing the product evidence and those details
+
+#### Scenario: Alternate is not distinct
+- **WHEN** the product-bearing text is identical to the normalized original tender line after canonicalization
+- **THEN** the system SHALL not make an additional retrieval request
+
+### Requirement: Conservative mixed-line recognition
+The system SHALL decline to create a product-bearing alternate unless both the work action and supported product anchor occur in the same unambiguous clause. It MUST NOT infer a product from service-only wording, substitute a product family, or remove explicit technical constraints from the extracted product text.
+
+#### Scenario: Service-only clause
+- **WHEN** a tender line contains a recognized work action but no supported product anchor
+- **THEN** the system SHALL preserve the existing retrieval behavior without creating a product-bearing alternate
+
+#### Scenario: Product line without work wording
+- **WHEN** a tender line names a supported product but contains no recognized work action
+- **THEN** the system SHALL preserve the existing canonicalization and retrieval behavior without applying product-span extraction
+
+#### Scenario: Ambiguous multi-clause line
+- **WHEN** the nearest product anchor cannot be associated with the work action in the same clause
+- **THEN** the system SHALL not create a product-bearing alternate
+
+### Requirement: Selection and availability preservation
+The product-bearing alternate SHALL affect candidate generation only. The system MUST retain the normalized original tender line as the reranking input and result query, preserve existing candidate limits and duplicate handling, and fail open to original-query candidates if alternate retrieval is unavailable.
+
+#### Scenario: Reranking a mixed line
+- **WHEN** an alternate is generated and retrieval succeeds
+- **THEN** the reranker and returned match result use the normalized original tender line
+
+#### Scenario: Alternate retrieval failure
+- **WHEN** retrieval of the product-bearing alternate raises an operational error
+- **THEN** the system SHALL continue with candidates retrieved from the original tender line
